2. llm-for-zotero
   Copyright (C) Yile Wang and contributors
   License: AGPL-3.0-or-later
   Source: https://github.com/yilewang/llm-for-zotero
   Pinned revision: d9724df84ac053343cf32b00c7829620a243e5b9
   (v3.8.30-4-gd9724df8)

   The legacy Codex authentication client and MinerU cache validation design
   were adapted from the upstream implementation patterns, notably
   src/utils/llmClient.ts, src/agent/model/codexResponses.ts,
   src/utils/providerTransport.ts, and its MinerU provenance/cache code.
   The multi-provider preference model, global active-model selection,
   OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint resolution, minimal request
   payload, streaming SSE parser, and informational connection test also
   adapt the design boundaries in src/utils/modelProviders.ts,
   src/utils/providerTransport.ts, src/utils/llmClient.ts, and
   src/modules/preferenceScript.ts at the pinned revision. This project keeps
   only Codex Auth and generic OpenAI Compatible modes in its initial API-key
   implementation; the original adaptation did not copy upstream provider-
   specific protocols or presets. Local-model, WebChat, Copilot, Gemini and
   App Server runtime branches remain outside this project.
   Version 1.2.0 also consults the Responses input_image conversion and data
   URL handling in src/utils/llmClient.ts, Reader document discovery in
   src/modules/contextPanel/readerSelection.ts, page-location conventions in
   src/modules/contextPanel/livePdfSelectionLocator.ts, MinerU figure metadata
   handling in src/modules/contextPanel/mineruFigureBlocks.ts, and the overlay
   interaction pattern in src/modules/contextPanel/screenshot.ts.

   Version 1.5.0 additionally consults revision
   7e26a134fe0808070d63df49a25ca9ba3bf031c9: src/utils/modelProviders.ts,
   src/utils/providerProtocol.ts, src/utils/providerTransport.ts,
   src/utils/apiHelpers.ts, src/utils/llmClient.ts and
   src/modules/preferenceScript.ts. The independently implemented adaptation
   adds explicit public Responses and Anthropic Messages transports, URL
   presets, protocol-specific image conversion and separate text/image tests.
   It does not reuse model-name inference, automatic protocol fallback,
   conversation state, file upload or provider-specific Agent runtimes.

   Version 1.5.2 adapts the collapsible provider-row interaction and layout
   from src/modules/preferenceScript.ts at the same reviewed revision
   7e26a134fe0808070d63df49a25ca9ba3bf031c9. It includes the unmodified
   addon/content/icons/providers/openai.svg, anthropic.svg and deepseek.svg
   assets from that revision. This adaptation does not share upstream runtime
   objects, provider preferences or credentials.

   Only the Reader interaction and coordinate-mapping patterns are reused for
   OCR. This project does not reuse screenshot.ts captureRegion, PDF canvas
   capture, drawWindow fallback, or PDF page rendering. It crops the local
   MinerU image asset that the validated cache metadata maps to the user's
   selected region.

No upstream runtime object, conversation, prompt, thread, or private source
file is accessed at runtime. Both plugins may read the user's Codex CLI login
file, but this plugin keeps its requests and paper context independent.

